# REFERENCE - @plurnk/plurnk-providers-ollama's shipped .env.defaults (ecosystem standard,
# providers#44: every package owns what it reads; the file IS the documentation). The daemon
# assembles every installed member's file into one floor, set-if-unset under the operator's env
# - do NOT edit this file; put YOUR config in ~/.plurnk/.env or ./.env. The PLURNK_PROVIDERS_*
# knobs ollama reads (REASONING, FETCH_TIMEOUT, RETRY_*) live in @plurnk/plurnk-providers' floor,
# not re-declared here (a key claimed by two packages crashes boot).

# --- Ollama endpoint (SPEC §5) ---
# Ships at the canonical local install: zero config for a stock `ollama serve`. Override in your
# .env for a LAN box, or per-alias with PLURNK_BASEURL_<alias> (which wins). The official
# OLLAMA_HOST is also read by the provider, but this floored OLLAMA_BASE_URL shadows it; point
# elsewhere via OLLAMA_BASE_URL or the per-alias override, not OLLAMA_HOST.
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
